GAL22V10
BRIDGE

CLK  AS   RW   JSEL RDY  FC0  FC1  FC2  A1   A2   A3   GND
RESET VPA IACK5 WBUF ABUF JDTACK LE ABR Q1   PHI2 Q0   VCC

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; MC68008 core board, GAL2: Junior/Elektor bus bridge and interrupt ack.
; Clocked by the 8 MHz CPU clock. All registers change on rising CLK.
;
; PHI2 = CLK/8: a free-running 1 MHz clock with 50% duty, locked to the
; CPU. State s = (PHI2,Q1,Q0) counts 0..7; PHI2 is high in states 4..7.
;
; A window cycle (JSEL low, from GAL1):
;  1. ABR (armed) is set on an edge into state 0, 1 or 2, so the bus
;     buffers only ever switch on while PHI2 is low, and at least 250 ns
;     before PHI2 rises. ABUF and WBUF enable the address buffers and, for
;     writes, the data buffer.
;  2. LE rises with PHI2 (edge 3 -> 4) when armed, and stays high for that
;     whole PHI2-high phase. The 74HCT573 read latch is transparent while LE
;     is high and latches as PHI2 falls. RAM.RW = /(LE * /RW) is made with
;     a 74LS01 open-collector NAND (plus a 74LS04 for /RW) and a pull-up,
;     as on the Junior.
;  3. On the PHI2 falling edge (7 -> 0), if RDY is high, JDTACK is
;     asserted. If RDY is low the access repeats in the next PHI2 phase.
;  4. AS rises: JSEL goes high, ABUF/WBUF switch off at once, JDTACK is
;     tri-stated and cleared on the next edge.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

AR       = /RESET

; 3-bit counter, PHI2 = CLK/8
Q0.R     = /Q0
Q1.R     = Q1 * /Q0
         + /Q1 * Q0
PHI2.R   = PHI2 * /Q1
         + PHI2 * /Q0
         + /PHI2 * Q1 * Q0

; Arm: set at an edge into state 0, 1 or 2 (from 7, 0 or 1), held while JSEL.
ABR.R    = /JSEL * ABR
         + /JSEL * PHI2 * Q1 * Q0
         + /JSEL * /PHI2 * /Q1

; Transfer window: rises with PHI2 (3 -> 4), held through states 5..7.
LE.R     = /JSEL * ABR * /PHI2 * Q1 * Q0 * JDTACK
         + LE * PHI2 * /Q1
         + LE * PHI2 * /Q0

; DTACK: asserted on the PHI2 falling edge (7 -> 0) if RDY.
/JDTACK.R = LE * PHI2 * Q1 * Q0 * RDY
          + /JDTACK * /JSEL
JDTACK.E = /JSEL

; Buffer enables (active low), off immediately when AS ends the cycle.
/ABUF    = /JSEL * ABR
/WBUF    = /JSEL * ABR * /RW

; Interrupt acknowledge. Level 5 (68681) gets its own vector via IACK5;
; levels 2 (bus IRQ) and 7 (bus NMI) are autovectored via VPA.
/IACK5   = /AS * FC2 * FC1 * FC0 * A3 * /A2 * A1
/VPA     = /AS * FC2 * FC1 * FC0 * /A3 * A2 * /A1
         + /AS * FC2 * FC1 * FC0 * A3 * A2 * A1

DESCRIPTION
68008 core board GAL2 (8 MHz): 1 MHz PHI2 and synchronous Junior bus
cycles (ABUF, WBUF, LE, DTACK with RDY), IACK5 and autovector VPA.
